    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d867">

                <pb facs="0861" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48/1061: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-31T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                                1919—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your 320, December 25, 10 a.m.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d867-f1"/></p>
                <p>Miller, Reval, telegraphs that due to
                    difficulty transshipping food supplies from Viborg to Reval, he desires to use
                    1,000 tons now at Reval for general and army relief. Department sees no
                    objection thereto, and if you concur, so instruct Miller.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
